# Build output. Every one of these is reproducible from source with west.
build/
build-*/
*.o
*.obj
*.d

# Guest images and firmware binaries. The tree is 2.9 GB with these in and
# ~2 MB without; they are build artifacts of the Buildroot recipe in BUILD.md,
# not sources. The known-good ELF archive is deliberately excluded too - it is
# a local recovery cache, and a stale "known-good" binary in git is worse than
# no binary at all (see known-good/README.txt).
*.elf
*.bin
*.ext2
*.uf2
*.img
# Kernel images anywhere. CAUTION, learned the expensive way: macOS git
# matches ignores case-insensitively (core.ignorecase=true), so a bare
# `Image` pattern also swallowed the entire ra8d1-linux/image/ DIRECTORY -
# every Buildroot recipe, config fragment and overlay silently never made it
# into the repo. The negation below re-includes the directory itself (last
# match wins; the trailing slash means it applies to the dir, not children),
# while Image* files inside stay ignored.
**/Image
**/Image-*
!ra8d1-linux/image/
rootfs
rootfs-*
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Serial captures and logs from bring-up runs.
*.log
!host-boot.log

# Upstream checkout, not our code: a pristine clone of
# https://github.com/cnlohr/mini-rv32ima at 84858f5 with no local
# modifications. Re-clone it there rather than vendoring a copy here.
ra8d1-linux/emulator/

# Local tooling noise
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.cache/
.DS_Store
compile_commands.json

# Not part of the Linux port story this repo tells. These exist in the local
# working tree (the Z80 arcade experiment, the CircuitPython bring-up pack and
# its runbook, the Slack coordination doc) but the repo is the record of
# bringing up Linux + Blinka on this board, and they are neither.
ra8d1-arcade/
ra8d1-pack/
ra8d1-cli.md
SLACK.md
